import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="About · Waynesville Daily Brief" showInfoBar={false}>
  <div class="reading">
    <p class="kicker">About</p>
    <h1>Waynesville Daily Brief</h1>
    <p class="dek">
      The Waynesville &amp; Warren County news you’d otherwise miss — schools first,
      plus the events that make this place worth living in.
    </p>

    <div class="callout">
      <strong>This is a demo build.</strong> The layout is real; most of the words are placeholders.
      Events are real, but the daily brief and headlines are illustrative and invent no names,
      quotes, or specific claims. Real, sourced reporting replaces them once daily publishing begins.
    </div>

    <h2>What makes this different</h2>
    <p>
      Warren County already has a template news feed. We aim to be better in three specific ways:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Schools first.</strong> Wayne Local news and Spartans sports lead every brief — that’s what this town actually opens its phone for.</li>
      <li><strong>A real events engine.</strong> This is a destination — the Waynesville Air Show, Fox Hollow Rodeo, the Ohio Renaissance Festival, Caesar Creek, the Little Miami Trail, Kings Island. We cover it as a curated, always-current calendar, not a scraped list.</li>
      <li><strong>Trust over volume.</strong> Every item is sourced and linked. We’d rather run five true, useful things than fifty scraped ones.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How it’s made</h2>
    <p>
      Each weekday, sources across Waynesville, Corwin, and Warren County are gathered and drafted into
      a brief. A human editor reviews and edits every edition before it publishes — nothing about a
      real person goes live without that review. Sources include Wayne Local Schools, the Village of
      Waynesville, the Warren County Commissioners, local event venues, and the National Weather Service.
    </p>

    <h2>Who’s behind it</h2>
    <p>
      Waynesville Daily Brief is written and edited locally. Story tips, corrections, and events are
      always welcome: <strong>editor@waynesville.news</strong>.
    </p>

    <p class="small"><a href="/">← Home</a></p>
  </div>
</Base>
